    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d564-a2">

                <pb facs="0570" n="472" sameAs="frus:frus1900/pg472"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Porter to the Secretary of the Rochambeau
                        Committee</hi>.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Embassy of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1900-03-28"><hi rendition="#italic">March 28,
                        1900</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>I have received your telegram announcing to me the laying of the capstone of the
                    monument to Rochambeau, and I gladly hasten to transmit to my Government the
                    fraternal greetings which you send to President McKinley and to the American
                    people. I congratulate you on having carried out your work to a good end and am
                    happy that you have had the idea to float the flag of my country side by side
                    with the national colors on the monument of a French soldier whose memory lives
                    in all American hearts.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Porter.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
